From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ecm_interface: fix the second multicast hierarchy row bound

0040 fixed one of a pair. ecm_interface_multicast_from_heirarchy_construct()
guards its second heirarchy_get() with

	if (valid_if > ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX)

where the sibling twenty lines of context earlier - the one 0040
corrected - uses >=. The interfaces buffer holds exactly
ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX rows, so valid_if == ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX
passes this guard and
ecm_db_multicast_if_heirarchy_get(interfaces, valid_if) returns the row
one past the end, which the code then writes a full interface hierarchy
into. Reached by a multicast group with exactly the maximum number of
destination interfaces.

With that closed, tighten the assert in the accessor as well.
ecm_db_multicast_if_heirarchy_get() asserted index <=
ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX against an allocation of exactly that many rows,
so it would have passed the bad index through rather than catching it.

Tightening a live DEBUG_ASSERT is only safe with the callers audited,
since ECM builds at debug level 1 and DEBUG_ASSERT is BUG() there. All
46 call sites were checked: every one is a loop bounded by
i < ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX, or passes a count already guarded < that
value - the two in ecm_interface.c by 0040 and by this change, and the
third by a DEBUG_ASSERT(valid_if < ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX) directly
above it. Nothing legitimate reaches the boundary value once the guard
above is corrected, so the tightened assert cannot fire on a path
multicast traffic drives.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

--- a/ecm_db/ecm_db_types.h
+++ b/ecm_db/ecm_db_types.h
@@ -481,7 +481,7 @@ static inline struct ecm_db_iface_instan
 {
 	unsigned long *heirarchy_instance = (unsigned long *)heirarchy_base;
 	DEBUG_ASSERT(heirarchy_instance, "Bad memory, multicast interfaces list has been already freed\n");
-	DEBUG_ASSERT((index <= ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX), "Bad index %u\n", index);
+	DEBUG_ASSERT((index < ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX), "Bad index %u\n", index);
 	return (struct ecm_db_iface_instance *)(heirarchy_instance + (index * ECM_DB_IFACE_HEIRARCHY_MAX));
 }
 
--- a/ecm_interface.c
+++ b/ecm_interface.c
@@ -5559,7 +5559,7 @@ int32_t ecm_interface_multicast_heirarch
 			return 0;
 		}
 
-		if (valid_if > ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX) {
+		if (valid_if >= ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX) {
 			int i;
 
 			/*
